- Open in Web IDE
- View Code
- View Git Changes
- View APIs
- View Logs
- Open DB Workbench
- View Runtime
- View Dependencies
- View Recent Changes
- Build
- Test
- Ask MIM Expert

Only show actions actually available for the selected service.

Reuse existing pages/tools instead of duplicating their functionality.
Deep-link them with current service context already selected.

5. Dependency / Impact View

Add an interactive service dependency section.

Show:
- upstream dependencies
- downstream consumers
- related APIs/events where discoverable.

Support natural-language impact questions such as:
“If this API/DTO/event changes, what can be impacted?”

Use current code/KB/dependency evidence and clearly separate:
confirmed dependencies
vs
possible/inferred impact.

Allow clicking a dependency to open its Service 360 page.

6. Runtime & Release Intelligence

Where data is available, correlate:

OpenShift deployed service
→ deployed image/version
→ Git tag/commit
→ recent code changes.

Allow questions such as:
“Did this issue start after the latest deployment?”
“What changed in the currently deployed release?”

