Pass selected service context automatically.

8. Profile Awareness

Reuse existing profiles:
Default, Developer, Tester, Business.

Developer:
emphasize code, dependencies, Git, APIs, DB, runtime, build/test.

Tester:
emphasize APIs, runtime, logs, DB state, expected behavior, test/regression information.

Business:
emphasize service purpose, business flow, impact, dependencies and health.
Hide low-level developer-only details unless explicitly requested.

Default:
balanced view.

Profile changes must update presentation immediately without changing underlying evidence.

9. “Ask About This”

Make major Service 360 elements context-aware.

For items such as:
API
dependency
deployment
log summary
DB collection
recent change

provide “Ask MIM Expert” capability.

Automatically attach the selected item + service context so the user can ask:
“Why is this important?”
“Show code for this.”
“Could this cause the current issue?”
“What consumes this API?”

10. Reliability

- All investigation access remains read-only.
- One failing integration must not block other sections.
- Clearly show Connected / Unavailable / Error states.
- Never expose credentials/tokens.
- Do not invent missing information.
- Show evidence/sources for AI conclusions.
- Preserve all existing functionality.

Target experience:

Select service
→ instantly see its complete 360° overview
→ ask normal-language questions
→ inspect runtime/code/logs/DB/APIs/dependencies
→ jump to the right tool with one click
→ return to Service 360 with context preserved.

Service 360 should become the central entry point for understanding and working with any MIM service.



